{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/282504-creative-structuring-help-wanted-for-new-chronicle","id":282504,"title":"Creative & Structuring Help Wanted for New Chronicle","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-10-15T10:50:51-07:00","id":282504,"title":"Creative & Structuring Help Wanted for New Chronicle","content":"I'm thinking of (finally!) starting up a Changeling game. I have a setting in mind (a rather small town somewhere North of Miami, named Coconut Bay), and I'm currently fleshing out characters &amp; NPCs, but I feel like my grip on the story is sub-optimal.<br /> I have this idea that the area is about to be the battleground/gameboard between 2 True Fae (The one who theoretically &quot;owns&quot; the area, both Faerie and mundane, and an aspiring usurper).<br /> The usurper's (The Queen of Broken Reflections) Realm is constantly moving, an expanse of freezing-cold water and mirror-ice centred on the rusty Soviet ice-breaker where she holds court. Her entire being is focused on a search for something (not even I am quite sure what).<br /> The current lord I have much less of a grip on, but I'm thinking something that fits well with sub-tropic jungle islands (which is what I imagine his Realm to be).<br /> <br /> The moment their Realms intersected each other, Arcadia shifted in such a way that quite a few Changelings managed to escape. Those who did stumbled out of various mirrors throughout Coconut Bay, looking like they did the moment they disappeared. They players all emerge in the same place, a mirror-lined park named Glittering Park, and at the same time.<br /> What lies around them is what used to be their home, leader-less about to be ravaged by supernatural forces.<br /> My idea is that Changelings are pretty new to this town, and as such there are no organized society for them (Courts and so on), but that the players will be the ones to introduce order and (hopefully) rally the disorganized (and sometimes warring) factions together to make a stand against their Keepers.<br /> <br /> Where I'm filled with uncertainty (apart from this being my first-ever Changeling campaign) is currently the start: How the PCs grasp the concepts (and benefits) of Courts, how they introduce it to others, and how to give them that push in the right direction that I know from experience that they need to get started.<br /> <br /> As bonus questions I'd like ideas for the Keeper who &quot;traditionally&quot; rules the area, and an estimate of how many differing factions (both mortal and fae) are required to fall between Just Enough and Not Too Many.<br /> <br /> Can provide a partial map of Coconut Beach, and hopefully more information about both town and characters, should there be need for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4096-lizardo","name":"Lizardo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T22:42:54-07:00","id":283410,"title":"","content":"How well the PCs grasp things really depends on how fresh they are. If they're straight from the Thorns, you might want to have some members of a current Freehold find and mentor them, if there is one (this would give them time to grow a bit into more established characters, the better to have things they care about that you can cruelly tear away from them whilst they weep). If you want them to have an idea of the Courts before they get out, maybe have one or more of them have spent time in Arcadia with a re-captured former escapee who might have explained the concepts with a greater or lesser degree of misremembered jumbling of concepts. <br /> <br /> Or maybe they find the shattered remains of the Hollow owned by the Freehold who *used* to hold the place - along with the apocalyptic log of how infighting and a breakdown of the traditions and exchange of power created an opening that the Shepherd of Swaying Palms exploited when his servants took over the place. <br /> <br /> As for the Shepherd, he styles himself as a revivalist minister of the sort that might go as a missionary to &quot;lesser&quot; peoples. His Realm takes the form of an infinite archipelago of small and medium-sized islands, all covered in palm trees driven by a constant wind. The island he uses as his main home is base to the Shepherd's church, a massive yet ramshackle building that plays host to spiritual meetings in praise of the Shepherd himself every day. His worshipers are culled from the slaves of other Keepers, taken in predatory tent evangelism excursions, or of his own captured faithful. The religious services he hosts are all fire and brimstone, full of driving music and mad glossolalia among the faithful. The Shepherd himself is a charismatic figure formed entirely of palm stalks and fronds, and he can see anything that happens within sight of any of the islands' trees. He is the forest, the church, the pastor, and the religion itself. <br /> <br /> On a side note, it's very difficult for the Others to rule areas of the Mortal World directly, as reality is so inimical to them. If they spend any real amount of time in the Real, they die or become Exiles. It might make more sense to have the area ruled and fought over by slaves and agents of the Keepers, with the bosses holding their own shadow conflict in Arcadia and the Hedge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}